01:16:55.923 --> 01:16:59.384
So today we're going to be talking about 27 transportation projects,

01:16:59.660 --> 01:17:02.568
kind of the methodology we use to come up with the 5-year capital plan.

01:17:03.510 --> 01:17:06.824
This is my first time with the budget cycle, as well as Chris.

01:17:06.940 --> 01:17:10.682
So we had a good time working together, working off the IFP and the

01:17:11.182 --> 01:17:14.618
Transportation Master Plan. And we spent a good time working in the software

01:17:14.635 --> 01:17:17.764
Planet to see what it can do for us, how it can help us with

01:17:18.264 --> 01:17:21.666
the budgeting. We ended up figuring out a good project delivery

01:17:21.715 --> 01:17:25.557
system where every year we're trying to have funding for design

01:17:25.670 --> 01:17:29.894
and construction. And we're trying to do it in a way so we're

01:17:30.394 --> 01:17:33.806
finishing up design— like right now we're finishing up design projects. And then for that

01:17:34.306 --> 01:17:37.661
design project, we have construction funding, the majority of it coming out of the next

01:17:38.161 --> 01:17:41.965
fiscal year. And in doing so, we can get a better estimate

01:17:41.981 --> 01:17:45.932
for the cost of the projects from the engineer's estimate from design instead of just

01:17:46.432 --> 01:17:50.284
going off of the IFP, which we use to plan for. And they're usually higher

01:17:50.429 --> 01:17:54.107
just from the nature of the projects. They use the standard UDOT template,

01:17:54.123 --> 01:17:57.159
so things are always kind of inflated a little bit, but that's a good thing

01:17:57.239 --> 01:18:00.595
for your, for your planning long range. But doing this delivery

01:18:00.627 --> 01:18:03.822
system, we're able to kind of sharpen the pencil and to know what the projects

01:18:04.322 --> 01:18:07.611
will actually cost us in the following fiscal year. So we've done that, and that's

01:18:08.111 --> 01:18:11.223
helped us save over $1.5 million on projects that we have coming up

01:18:11.723 --> 01:18:14.915
for design this construction season. And it's also helped

01:18:15.415 --> 01:18:18.463
us to find projects that are underfunded. We found there was one I'll talk about

01:18:18.963 --> 01:18:21.754
that was underestimated in the IFP.

01:18:22.798 --> 01:18:25.591
So the first project we have is SR 73.

01:18:26.217 --> 01:18:29.510
and Ranches, and then the high-T intersection at Campus

01:18:30.010 --> 01:18:33.558
