01:40:48.858 --> 01:40:52.544
for reimbursement. Yep.

01:40:53.665 --> 01:40:57.092
Next one is Pole Canyon and Pony Express Parkway. We're seeing a

01:40:57.592 --> 01:41:01.154
lot of traffic, not just from residents but from commercial as well. at this intersection.

01:41:01.973 --> 01:41:05.363
The current intersection is already really goofy aligned the

01:41:05.863 --> 01:41:09.539
way it is. Here's Pole Canyon. The pavement doesn't even align in

01:41:10.039 --> 01:41:14.085
its current configuration. There's no deceleration lanes currently on

01:41:14.117 --> 01:41:17.538
Pony Express, so the traffic here slows down immensely in the morning.

01:41:18.213 --> 01:41:21.827
And then in, in the evening, the lefts trying to get out can

01:41:22.327 --> 01:41:25.730
never make it with this traffic heading northbound. I've seen vehicles driving the dirt road

01:41:26.230 --> 01:41:29.375
here and cut across traffic, all kinds of shady stuff out there. So it's just—

01:41:29.760 --> 01:41:31.719
and the worst thing is a lot of this we know are, you know,

01:41:32.088 --> 01:41:36.038
from construction, but you have residents trying to come home, going over to Scarlet

01:41:36.538 --> 01:41:38.527
Ridge Parkway Fields, and they're fighting this traffic.

01:41:39.346 --> 01:41:42.846
So what this project would do is it would widen the intersection. The rest

01:41:43.346 --> 01:41:46.604
of the road would come with development, but for now we would widen the intersection

01:41:46.732 --> 01:41:50.762
so it properly aligns. We'd have a deceleration lane here, traffic signal,

01:41:51.213 --> 01:41:54.680
With again the priority being the north-south movement, but it would still have those protected

01:41:55.180 --> 01:41:58.854
lefts. So the widening there,

01:41:58.903 --> 01:42:02.475
you're going to try to accommodate a couple left-hand turn lanes

01:42:02.604 --> 01:42:05.934
to be able to turn onto Bonney Express? That's okay. Yep. And that's,

01:42:06.804 --> 01:42:10.045
uh, eastbound traffic to northbound traffic? Correct.

01:42:10.190 --> 01:42:13.621
Yep, east to north. Yep. I mean, we need to widen it so much because

01:42:13.654 --> 01:42:16.865
the current left lane is here, and so we need to get it fully widened

01:42:17.365 --> 01:42:20.262
And so they line up, because you don't want lefts offset. That creates blind spots

01:42:20.311 --> 01:42:22.840
and hazards for turning, and you can't see oncoming traffic.

01:42:23.615 --> 01:42:26.241
So it makes sense to do the whole full widening and fix it now than

01:42:26.741 --> 01:42:28.562
just, oh, we'll do this later and this later. No, we should fix it and

01:42:29.062 --> 01:42:32.187
fix it right. And then later development can widen it, you know, and do the

01:42:32.687 --> 01:42:36.156
full section later on. So for that project, we're asking

01:42:36.172 --> 01:42:39.278
for design funds so we can get started on design. And then same thing,

01:42:39.326 --> 01:42:42.351
we can look at 28 when we come back and kind of sharpen the pencil

01:42:42.516 --> 01:42:46.322
I ran this estimate, and then what does that look like, uh, going forward for

01:42:46.822 --> 01:42:50.255
the next fiscal year? Uh, just to— it's probably

01:42:50.755 --> 01:42:53.146
not a question for you, maybe for— is Brandon here?

01:42:53.852 --> 01:42:56.790
Brandon, that section that's to the west of that intersection,

01:42:56.823 --> 01:42:59.183
Pole Canyon Road, Pony Express,

01:42:59.938 --> 01:43:03.647
do we have any idea development-wise when we are— we

01:43:04.147 --> 01:43:06.697
will start to see that develop on the other side of the road where we

01:43:07.197 --> 01:43:10.323
can have participation from the developer? Or are we so far out on that that

01:43:10.823 --> 01:43:13.114
it's, it's really just going to be an intersection and it's going to sit there

01:43:13.614 --> 01:43:16.530
for a while? And I'll let him answer that, but I do know Firefly has

01:43:16.578 --> 01:43:19.705
a lot of that roadway that's in there. All the way to the Pony Express?

01:43:19.769 --> 01:43:23.666
I believe it's all the way to Pony Express. I haven't heard anything

01:43:23.779 --> 01:43:27.547
from them about developing that road anytime soon. So maybe

01:43:28.047 --> 01:43:30.274
this is one of those opportunities for us to work out a deal with them

01:43:30.774 --> 01:43:33.935
to get the road that we need to be built in exchange for some something

01:43:33.968 --> 01:43:37.403
that's of benefit to them so we can have the road available for the use

01:43:37.903 --> 01:43:39.829
of our citizens. Would be helpful. They could use it.

01:43:43.701 --> 01:43:46.879
So my last one is Mount Airy widening. This is

01:43:46.976 --> 01:43:50.381
one that would remove the medians on Mount

01:43:50.445 --> 01:43:53.705
Airy to SR 73. Currently the medians go from Mount

01:43:53.753 --> 01:43:58.094
Airy down here to, uh, Inverness. And what we're seeing is because

01:43:58.272 --> 01:44:01.645
there's only one lane at

01:44:02.145 --> 01:44:05.418
the intersection. The lefts are blocking the right movements in the morning, and so cars

01:44:05.450 --> 01:44:09.120
know that, and so they blow through this neighborhood and take this right and right

01:44:09.620 --> 01:44:12.629
out with acceleration lane. What we want to do is remove this median,

01:44:13.447 --> 01:44:17.084
make 2 lanes here, so this is the more appealing traffic that will eventually

01:44:17.148 --> 01:44:20.401
divert traffic. And we talk about speed management,

01:44:20.417 --> 01:44:23.558
you know, Chief Knutson was talking about, and, you know, stop signs are not a

01:44:24.058 --> 01:44:27.063
great way to manage speed or speed humps. The best way to fix speed is

01:44:27.096 --> 01:44:30.441
geometry, is making roads more appealing, or to restrict,

01:44:30.635 --> 01:44:34.235
you know, roads with striping or other features. This would help alleviate

01:44:34.735 --> 01:44:37.527
a lot of that potential traffic that's blowing through this neighborhood by making this the

01:44:38.027 --> 01:44:41.015
ideal road, because you can continue straight and hop on the highway faster.

01:44:41.563 --> 01:44:43.960
So that's one way we want to kind of propose this project.

01:44:45.210 --> 01:44:48.243
We're asking for design funds to kind of get going on this, and then same

01:44:48.324 --> 01:44:50.379
thing, looking at construction for the following year.

